Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 18:42:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] platform/surface: aggregator_registry: Use the POS tablet
 switch on Surface Pro 11

The ACPI tables of the Surface Pro 11 declare two Surface hot-plug
devices, both created from the same driver, with different feature
words returned by _DSM function 6: the KIP instance (\_SB.SHPS) returns
0x080E and the SAM instance (\_SB.WSID.SHPS) returns 0x060C. The laptop
and slate indicator (\_SB.SLT, MSHW0005) is fed by the SAM instance,
which reads the device posture (POS, target category 0x26), while the
KIP instance only follows the cover state and is barred from the
indicator.

Register the POS tablet switch as on the other models that report their
posture through POS, instead of the KIP one.

Local status: held pending local posture/resume evidence and cross-check.
An independent upstream report proposes the same switch:
https://lkml.iu.edu/2609.2/08840.html
The feature-word interpretation above remains an inherited REA lead.

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5
Assisted-by: Codex gpt-6.1-sol
---
 drivers/platform/surface/surface_aggregator_registry.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/platform/surface/surface_aggregator_registry.c b/drivers/platform/surface/surface_aggregator_registry.c
index 990587985..df6b57055 100644
--- a/drivers/platform/surface/surface_aggregator_registry.c
+++ b/drivers/platform/surface/surface_aggregator_registry.c
@@ -415,7 +415,7 @@ static const struct software_node *ssam_node_group_sp11[] = {
 	&ssam_node_hid_kip_keyboard,
 	&ssam_node_hid_kip_touchpad,
 	&ssam_node_hid_kip_fwupd,
-	&ssam_node_kip_tablet_switch,
+	&ssam_node_pos_tablet_switch,
 	NULL,
 };
 
